// full Prompt/Result move behind a "See input & output" toggle). One user prompt, one agent
// turn, THREE Stages (different owning assistant message ids, so `groupSubagentStages.ts`
// flushes a new Stage on the `messageId` change even with nothing else between them):
//
// Stage A ("solo-task", msg-a1): ONE agent ("SoloSweep"), NO batch `context` at all -- the
// scenario `StageGroupRow`'s solo branch needs `group.context` falsy for: `StageContextBrief`
// never renders, so the Stage level renders `SubagentGoalPreview` from `item.task` instead (gate
// round 1 fix, item 7: ordered before "Uses:", the same position a context-bearing Stage's own
// `StageContextBrief` takes). Its own task is deliberately a MULTI-LINE brief with a leading
// "# Goal" heading (the same heading-only-line convention `stageMeta.ts`'s own
// `extractContextLabel`/`extractTaskGoalPreview` already strip) and several further lines, long
// enough to genuinely overflow a `line-clamp-3` paragraph at a normal composer width -- proves
// the clamp is a real CSS constraint, not a component that merely never renders more than 3
// lines of text in the first place. A deliberate `{"__delay__":2500}` between the assistant-
// message echo and `tool_execution_end` keeps it OBSERVABLY running (no `item.result` yet) for a
// live check to confirm the toggle link reads "See input" (not "...& output") before it settles.
//
// Stage B ("members-task", msg-a2): TWO agents ("MemberOne", "MemberTwo") sharing ONE batch
// `context` -- the scenario a multi-agent Stage needs to prove no per-member goal duplication:
// `StageContextBrief` shows the shared goal once, each member's own `SubagentBody` shows none of
// its own (`showGoal={!item.context}`, both members' own calls carry no context of their own,
// gate round 1 fix item 1), and each member keeps its own INDEPENDENT toggle open/closed state.
//
// Stage C ("flat-task", msg-a3): TWO agents ("FlatOne", "FlatTwo"), NO batch `context` at all --
// gate round 1 fix, item 1's own live step: "a context-less multi-agent Stage (a flat call)
// shows each member's goal". With no shared context to lean on, `showGoal={!item.context}`
// resolves `true` for BOTH members (neither has its own), so each shows its own goal from its
// own distinct task, independently of its sibling.
//
// The final assistant text message includes a tiny Mermaid fenced block (gate round 1 fix, item
// 8: "MermaidBlock now gets Escape and a focus ring" -- `Markdown.tsx`'s `MermaidBlock` was
// ported onto the same shared `InlineDisclosure` this issue built, so its own "Show source"
// toggle gains both for free; this live-checks that directly rather than only by inspection).
